### 3. Memory Health Check
Is the user model (`agent.md`) up to date? Any stale facts to prune?

### 4. Pending Work
What's left unfinished or blocked?

### 5. Prompt Issues
Did a system-prompt template's *wording* make you misread an instruction, miss a
constraint, or take a wrong approach this session? If the cause was the template
itself being unclear or misleading — not just a slip on your part — flag it so
the prompt can improve. You don't need a long repeating pattern; one clear case
where the template's phrasing tripped you is enough to note. Emit a
`<prompt_issue>` block naming the offending template (e.g. `core_agent_system`,
`nova_review`), describing what was unclear and the behaviour it caused. Only
skip when nothing in the prompt wording genuinely got in your way.

Keep it concise — this is a checkpoint, not a full summary.

### Output Format
Record learnings in XML blocks. Omit empty blocks.

- `<user_model>` — user model entries (each as `## Section Header`). Merged into `agent.md` (always in context).
- `<lesson topic="...">` — cross-session decisions, patterns, facts as bullets, grouped under a short kebab-case `topic`. Written to `memories/<topic>.md` and indexed (surfaced in context via the memory INDEX). Emit one block per topic.
- `<skill>` — at most one. Only if step 2 identified a genuinely reusable workflow.
- `<habit>` — at most one. Only on a clean win (step 2b): 1-2 bullets of reusable good-practice guidance. Written to `HABITS.md` (always injected). Omit unless genuinely notable.
- `<prompt_issue template="...">` — per step 5, when a system-prompt template's wording caused a misread or wrong approach this session. One short paragraph: what was unclear + the behaviour it caused.

